\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Figure: Hierarchical diagnostics for speech representation quality. The suite organizes (1) phonetic discriminability/invariance via fast ABX with MFCC baselines, PanPhon correlations, layer-wise profiles, and snippet sweeps to expose leakage across factors; (2) decoder-free token stability and linguistic alignment using TER/MTER under controlled WORLD prosody edits, segment-restricted TER for emphasis, PNMI, and PAST operating points to select layer/rate–latency–fidelity trade-offs; and (3) beyond-semantic competence and robustness through BoSS affect/dialect probes and SALMON consistency/alignment tasks, extensible to broader multilingual ASR/SID/LID/KWS/QbE coverage.}}{20}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tiny_tree_figure_1}{{3}{20}{Figure: Hierarchical diagnostics for speech representation quality. The suite organizes (1) phonetic discriminability/invariance via fast ABX with MFCC baselines, PanPhon correlations, layer-wise profiles, and snippet sweeps to expose leakage across factors; (2) decoder-free token stability and linguistic alignment using TER/MTER under controlled WORLD prosody edits, segment-restricted TER for emphasis, PNMI, and PAST operating points to select layer/rate–latency–fidelity trade-offs; and (3) beyond-semantic competence and robustness through BoSS affect/dialect probes and SALMON consistency/alignment tasks, extensible to broader multilingual ASR/SID/LID/KWS/QbE coverage}{figure.caption.4}{}}
